---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Advertising Disclosure"
  description="How NoCharge handles optional Adsterra banners, sponsored Smartlink no-fill links, consent, and ad reports."
  path="/advertising/"
  showAds={false}
>
  <article class="trust-page prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Advertising Disclosure' }]} />
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Advertising Disclosure</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">How advertising works on NoCharge.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Advertising is optional, labeled, separated from game play, and never required to understand a game.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-relationship">
      <h2 id="ads-relationship">Adsterra banner relationship</h2>
      <p>
        If you allow advertising, NoCharge may display banner advertising supplied through Adsterra. Those banners
        are third-party advertising, not NoCharge editorial content. Advertising consent is required before
        NoCharge requests ad frames or the related provider content.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-consent">
      <h2 id="ads-consent">Your advertising choice</h2>
      <p>
        Advertising is off by default. You can allow it through the consent banner or Privacy choices dialog, and
        withdraw it at any time through the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy page</a> or the footer’s Privacy choices
        button. Withdrawing consent hides ad placements and stops future optional advertising requests initiated by
        NoCharge in that tab.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-smartlink">
      <h2 id="ads-smartlink">Sponsored Smartlink no-fill fallback</h2>
      <p>
        If an allowed Adsterra banner does not fill, NoCharge may show a clearly labeled sponsored link as a
        no-fill fallback. It is not shown before advertising consent, does not open on its own, and opens only
        after you choose the labeled link. The destination is external and may change under the advertising
        provider’s control.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-labeling">
      <h2 id="ads-labeling">Labels, external destinations, and endorsement</h2>
      <p>
        Sponsored links are labeled, and advertising frames are identified as advertisements. An advertisement or
        external link does not mean NoCharge endorses, verifies, or guarantees the destination, offer, product,
        service, safety, availability, or claims made there. Use your own judgment and review an external site’s
        terms and privacy information before interacting with it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-isolation">
      <h2 id="ads-isolation">No ads over active gameplay</h2>
      <p>
        NoCharge does not place advertising over an active game viewport. Ads are outside the interactive game
        area, and shared full-screen or immersive game mode contains only the game viewport and its controls.
        Advertising is isolated in sandboxed frames. NoCharge does not trigger automatic top-level redirects to an
        advertiser or Smartlink destination.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-report">
      <h2 id="ads-report">Report a problematic advertisement</h2>
      <p>
        If you see an advertisement or sponsored destination that appears harmful, misleading, inappropriate, or
        broken, email <a href="mailto:hello@nocharge.net">hello@nocharge.net</a>. If possible, include the page
        where it appeared, the approximate date and time, and a description or screenshot. Do not send sensitive
        personal information. Reports help us review the placement, but we cannot guarantee an external provider’s
        response or content removal.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trust-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .trust-page > header {
    padding: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trust-page section {
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .trust-page section + section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
